<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Da Cruz family</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Da Cruz family were an Afro-Portuguese dynasty of prazo holders on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a>. From their fortified base at Massangano, above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tete">Tete</a>, they commanded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chikunda">Chikunda</a> soldiers, taxed river trade and raided for slaves and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-vicente-da-cruz">António Vicente da Cruz</a>, known as Bonga, they defied Portugal in the mid-nineteenth century, and their power was finally broken by Portuguese campaigns in 1888.</p></div>
